From: Local RE-CS-02 maintenance
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: constrain malformed CN upper-5GHz rule

On JDCloud RE-CS-02, ath11k submits a QCN9074 CN rule for
5735-5835 MHz with max bandwidth 160 MHz. cfg80211 rejects the entire
regdomain because bandwidth exceeds the 100 MHz frequency span.
The malformed submitted rule was captured with firmware WLAN.HK.2.15.
Raw WMI was not captured; firmware versus parsing responsibility is unresolved. The device's
stock WLAN.HK.2.5.r4 also failed CN, without a per-rule trace. A RAM-only
diagnostic on the installed module captured
the offending rule; a narrowly scoped 80 MHz correction permits CN.

Correct only this exact malformed rule on the copied regdomain before
submission. Do not change country, frequencies, power or DFS flags.
This source patch is provided for rebuilding; the accompanying live
validation used a version-pinned module shim, not a source-built image.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
@@ -286,6 +286,20 @@ int ath11k_regd_update(struct ath11k *ar)
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	if (regd_copy->alpha2[0] == 'C' && regd_copy->alpha2[1] == 'N') {
+		unsigned int i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < regd_copy->n_reg_rules; i++) {
+			struct ieee80211_freq_range *range;
+
+			range = &regd_copy->reg_rules[i].freq_range;
+			if (range->start_freq_khz == MHZ_TO_KHZ(5735) &&
+			    range->end_freq_khz == MHZ_TO_KHZ(5835) &&
+			    range->max_bandwidth_khz == MHZ_TO_KHZ(160))
+				range->max_bandwidth_khz = MHZ_TO_KHZ(80);
+		}
+	}
+
 	ret = regulatory_set_wiphy_regd(ar->hw->wiphy, regd_copy);
 
 	kfree(regd_copy);
